trol. Brains and Machines Brains and Machines Will Photonics Loosen the Bottlenecks in Neural Systems? photonics neuromorphic low latency WDM SOA WDM (Wavelength Division Multiplexing) Semiconductor Optical Amplifier (SOA) McCulloch-Pitts neuron model Indium Phosphide (InP) Femtojoule per operation TDM (Time Division Multiplexing)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-24-brainsandmachi-光子计算第三次浪潮-五年内走出实验室-先征服无人机/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/9151fd6dae1293cb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"B\"><span class=\"dur\">45:49</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Brains and Machines</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0824</span></div>\n<h2>Photonics&#x27; Third Wave: Out of the Lab in Five Years, Conquering Drones First</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Photons cannot interact like electrons, but wavelength multiplexing enables massive parallelism and ultra-low latency. All-optical neural networks could land within five years, with the first stop not servers but drones and real-time control.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">photonics</span><span class=\"tag\">neuromorphic</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"The Solid State Transformer Has Been Hyped for Fifty Years; AI Data Centers Are Its First Real Buyer The solid state transformer failed three times over — in the navy, in high-speed rail, in the smart grid — because all it offered was ‘smaller’. The copper problem and the 800-volt DC problem inside AI data centers are the first reasons it has ever had to exist. Asianometry Asianometry Has the Solid State Transformer’s Time Finally Come? Power electronics Data center power Solid state transformers 800V DC Silicon carbide Startup funding Solid State Transformer (SST) IGBT Silicon Carbide (SiC) Galvanic isolation 800VDC architecture PETT\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-24-asianometry-固态变压器吹了五十年-ai数据中心是第一个真买家/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/a4d5049243d5f237-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0824</span></div>\n<h2>The Solid State Transformer Has Been Hyped for Fifty Years; AI Data Centers Are Its First Real Buyer</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The solid state transformer failed three times over — in the navy, in high-speed rail, in the smart grid — because all it offered was ‘smaller’. The copper problem and the 800-volt DC problem inside AI data centers are the first reasons it has ever had to exist.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Power electronics</span><span class=\"tag\">Data center power</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"A Pitch Tells Two Stories: The Project, And The Buyer&#x27;s Promotion Hollywood screenwriter Rhett Reese on what a pitch actually is: the project story runs on the surface, the story of the other person&#x27;s success runs underneath. Make them the protagonist, lower their risk, enlarge their reward, and your pitch lands far more often. Think Fast Talk Smart Think Fast Talk Smart 317. Plot Twist: The Second Story Hiding Inside Every Great Pitch Pitching Communication Hollywood AI Collaboration pitch gatekeeper auteur\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-24-thinkfast-好提案藏着两个故事-你的故事和对方升职的故事/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7fd7a03d438b4365-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">24:09</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Think Fast Talk Smart</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0824</span>